  "generated_text": "1. **Prime Factorization**:\n   - $168 = 2^3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7$\n   - $693 = 3^2 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11$\n\n2. **Common Prime Factors**:\n   - The common prime factors are $3$ and $7$.\n\n3. **Smallest GCD**:\n   - The smallest possible value of $\\gcd(b,c)$ is the product of the common prime factors, which is $3 \\cdot 7 = 21$.\n\n4. **Conclusion**:\n   - The smallest possible value of $\\gcd(b,c)$ is $\\boxed{21}$.",
